      "duration": 2.72,
      "text": "hundreds of MIT courses, visit MITOpenCourseWare@ocw.mit.edu."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 21.51,
      "end": 29.8,
      "duration": 8.29,
      "text": "PROFESSOR:So lecture one, introduction."
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 39.98,
      "end": 42.52,
      "duration": 2.54,
      "text": "When people teach biology at different universities, they"
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 42.52,
      "end": 46.23,
      "duration": 3.71,
      "text": "teach many different things."
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 46.23,
      "end": 48.78,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "You could focus on the ecosystem."
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 48.78,
      "end": 52.3,
      "duration": 3.52,
      "text": "You could focus on memorizing different phyla."
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 52.3,
      "end": 54.17,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "You could focus on many things."
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 54.17,
      "end": 56.37,
      "duration": 2.2,
      "text": "Biology is huge and diverse."
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 56.37,
      "end": 58.95,
      "duration": 2.58,
      "text": "We have a certain point of view in the way we teach"
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 58.95,
      "end": 62.45,
      "duration": 3.5,
      "text": "7.012, and really a point of view in the way that MIT"
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 62.45,
      "end": 64.68,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "organizes its biology."
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 64.68,
      "end": 70.18,
      "duration": 5.5,
      "text": "And so I want to point out the levels of organization of life"
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 70.18,
      "end": 72.44,
      "duration": 2.26,
      "text": "and indicate where we will be."
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 77.51,
      "end": 81.06,
      "duration": 3.55,
      "text": "You could decide to study the entire biosphere."
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 83.56,
      "end": 86.57,
      "duration": 3.01,
      "text": "By the biosphere, I mean everything."
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 86.57,
      "end": 94.42,
      "duration": 7.85,
      "text": "All the world's ecosystems working together to create a"
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 94.42,
      "end": 97.4,
      "duration": 2.98,
      "text": "happy, healthy living planet."
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 97.4,
      "end": 103.57,
      "duration": 6.17,
      "text": "There are, oh I don't know, something like 10 to the sixth"
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 103.57,
      "end": 108.64,
      "duration": 5.07,
      "text": "eukaryotic species on this planet, more than a million"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 108.64,
      "end": 111.88,
      "duration": 3.24,
      "text": "species of things you can see with your eye, and there are"
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 111.88,
      "end": 115.69,
      "duration": 3.81,
      "text": "10 to the God knows how many species of microbes."
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 115.69,
      "end": 119.18,
      "duration": 3.49,
      "text": "And in fact, it's even hard to define species for microbes."
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 119.18,
      "end": 122.18,
      "duration": 3.0,
      "text": "So it's a fantastic diversity."
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 122.18,
      "end": 126.32,
      "duration": 4.14,
      "text": "And if we think about examples, the number of"
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 126.32,
      "end": 132.94,
      "duration": 6.62,
      "text": "examples of biospheres that we are aware of is one."
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 132.94,
      "end": 135.02,
      "duration": 2.08,
      "text": "Currently, it's the earth."
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 135.02,
      "end": 137.16,
      "duration": 2.14,
      "text": "There might be other biospheres, but we're not"
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 137.16,
      "end": 138.78,
      "duration": 1.62,
      "text": "aware of them."
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 138.78,
      "end": 142.11,
      "duration": 3.33,
      "text": "Alright, that's one level of organization."
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 142.11,
      "end": 144.42,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "We will have virtually nothing to say about that level of"
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 144.42,
      "end": 149.2,
      "duration": 4.78,
      "text": "organization other than that we're fond of it."
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 149.2,
      "end": 151.143,
      "duration": 1.943,
      "text": "Next, you can study an ecosystem."
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 155.11,
      "end": 156.85,
      "duration": 1.74,
      "text": "Now what do we mean by ecosystem?"
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 156.85,
      "end": 174.17,
      "duration": 17.32,
      "text": "That's some interacting community of organisms, like a"
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 174.17,
      "end": 177.7,
      "duration": 3.53,
      "text": "forest, let's say."
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 177.7,
      "end": 181.97,
      "duration": 4.27,
      "text": "You've got trees, and you've got, oh I don't"
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 181.97,
      "end": 185.53,
      "duration": 3.56,
      "text": "know, mice and deer."
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 185.53,
      "end": 188.78,
      "duration": 3.25,
      "text": "And you've got fungi growing down there on the bottom, and"
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 188.78,
      "end": 192.92,
      "duration": 4.14,
      "text": "maybe you have, I don't know, some MIT student walking"
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 192.92,
      "end": 194.88,
      "duration": 1.96,
      "text": "through the forest or something like that."
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 194.88,
      "end": 197.62,
      "duration": 2.74,
      "text": "That's all part of the ecosystem."
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 197.62,
      "end": 202.0,
      "duration": 4.38,
      "text": "Alright, now the next level down you could think about is"
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 202.0,
      "end": 203.25,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "whole organisms."
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 206.27,
      "end": 210.99,
      "duration": 4.72,
      "text": "So here we're talking about one individual, an individual"
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 210.99,
      "end": 212.24,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "in a species."
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 216.14,
      "end": 218.38,
      "duration": 2.24,
      "text": "And one can study how does that individual work, the"
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 218.38,
      "end": 223.35,
      "duration": 4.97,
      "text": "levels of physiology within an organism, the overall"
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 223.35,
      "end": 228.25,
      "duration": 4.9,
      "text": "integration of signals, the distribution of oxygen across"
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 228.25,
      "end": 229.57,
      "duration": 1.32,
      "text": "the body, things like that."
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 229.57,
      "end": 231.64,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "This is a popular topic to study."
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 231.64,
      "end": 237.94,
      "duration": 6.3,
      "text": "We'll have a little bit to say about physiology, but that"
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 237.94,
      "end": 241.0,
      "duration": 3.06,
      "text": "won't be our major focus, that whole organismal level of"
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 241.0,
      "end": 241.97,
      "duration": 0.97,
      "text": "physiology."
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 241.97,
      "end": 245.76,
      "duration": 3.79,
      "text": "Example of an organism, say a human, in particular, let's"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 245.76,
      "end": 247.73,
      "duration": 1.97,
      "text": "say an MIT student."
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 247.73,
      "end": 249.09,
      "duration": 1.36,
      "text": "OK."
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 249.09,
      "end": 257.22,
      "duration": 8.13,
      "text": "Next up, we could study an individual organ."
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 261.079,
      "end": 264.48,
      "duration": 3.401,
      "text": "So by an organ, I'm thinking about some part of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 264.48,
      "end": 267.97,
      "duration": 3.49,
      "text": "organism that's a group of tissues that are organized"
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 267.97,
      "end": 270.39,
      "duration": 2.42,
      "text": "together to carry out a function."
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 270.39,
      "end": 276.54,
      "duration": 6.15,
      "text": "So it's a group of tissues that are organized to carry"
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 276.54,
      "end": 277.79,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "out a function."
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 283.31,
      "end": 289.4,
      "duration": 6.09,
      "text": "And we have the eye, the eye on that human."
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 289.4,
      "end": 293.62,
      "duration": 4.22,
      "text": "So we've got these muscles here."
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 293.62,
      "end": 297.79,
      "duration": 4.17,
      "text": "We've got some photoreceptors there on the back, and they"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 297.79,
      "end": 301.92,
      "duration": 4.13,
      "text": "send back nerve terminals going there."
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 301.92,
      "end": 306.4,
      "duration": 4.48,
      "text": "All these tissues working together to provide vision."
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 306.4,
      "end": 307.13,
      "duration": 0.73,
      "text": "OK."
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 307.13,
      "end": 309.04,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "Going down one level below that we have tissues."
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 312.36,
      "end": 315.39,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "These are more homogeneous groups of cells."
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 319.61,
      "end": 328.08,
      "duration": 8.47,
      "text": "So we could have, say, the retina."
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 332.28,
      "end": 335.79,
      "duration": 3.51,
      "text": "Then those tissues are made up of cells."
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 339.23,
      "end": 345.45,
      "duration": 6.22,
      "text": "So cells of course are bounded by a membrane."
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 345.45,
      "end": 347.84,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "They have nuclei, at least in eukaryotes."
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 351.83,
      "end": 355.13,
      "duration": 3.3,
      "text": "So let's say within the retina, we could pick a"
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 355.13,
      "end": 356.6,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "photoreceptor cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 359.11,
      "end": 363.35,
      "duration": 4.24,
      "text": "So the MIT student is walking through the forest and with"
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 363.35,
      "end": 366.54,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "her eye is getting light on the retina, which is"
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 366.54,
      "end": 368.65,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "triggering photoreceptor cells."
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 368.65,
      "end": 375.66,
      "duration": 7.01,
      "text": "They each have a distinctive shape, and that shape--"
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 375.66,
      "end": 378.79,
      "duration": 3.13,
      "text": "there's our nucleus."
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 378.79,
      "end": 382.02,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "The light comes and impinges there, sends a signal"
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 382.02,
      "end": 383.465,
      "duration": 1.445,
      "text": "out the other end."
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 383.465,
      "end": 383.87,
      "duration": 0.405,
      "text": "OK."
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 383.87,
      "end": 386.12,
      "duration": 2.25,
      "text": "That's a cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 386.12,
      "end": 389.805,
      "duration": 3.685,
      "text": "Then we get down to organelles."
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 394.25,
      "end": 397.61,
      "duration": 3.36,
      "text": "These are distinct components within a cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 406.19,
      "end": 409.39,
      "duration": 3.2,
      "text": "For example, this photoreceptor is using up a"
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 409.39,
      "end": 411.49,
      "duration": 2.1,
      "text": "lot of energy."
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 411.49,
      "end": 412.74,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "It has mitochondria."
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 416.39,
      "end": 425.66,
      "duration": 9.27,
      "text": "These mitochondria in here are involved in producing"
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 425.66,
      "end": 428.99,
      "duration": 3.33,
      "text": "efficiently ATP."
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 428.99,
      "end": 432.165,
      "duration": 3.175,
      "text": "And then finally, we have molecules."
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 441.255,
      "end": 444.635,
      "duration": 3.38,
      "text": "A wide variety of different molecules in the cell: sugars"
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 444.635,
      "end": 449.68,
      "duration": 5.045,
      "text": "and DNA's and-- but I'll say ATP will be our example here."
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 449.68,
      "end": 450.63,
      "duration": 0.95,
      "text": "Molecules."
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 450.63,
      "end": 453.67,
      "duration": 3.04,
      "text": "So if you think about it, we have sets of levels of"
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 453.67,
      "end": 456.34,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "organization, all the way up there from biospheres to"
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 456.34,
      "end": 458.772,
      "duration": 2.432,
      "text": "ecosystems to organisms to organs to tissues to cells to"
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 458.772,
      "end": 460.33,
      "duration": 1.558,
      "text": "organelles to molecules."
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 460.33,
      "end": 463.24,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "And biology thinks about all of those different levels, and"
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 463.24,
      "end": 466.02,
      "duration": 2.78,
      "text": "in principle, they all interact."
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 466.02,
      "end": 469.23,
      "duration": 3.21,
      "text": "Of course, it's somewhat hard to keep in mind, say, the"
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 469.23,
      "end": 472.55,
      "duration": 3.32,
      "text": "connection between the entire biosphere and a ATP at any"
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 472.55,
      "end": 473.24,
      "duration": 0.69,
      "text": "given point."
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 473.24,
      "end": 475.91,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "It's a bunch of levels going up and down."
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 475.91,
      "end": 479.625,
      "duration": 3.715,
      "text": "At MIT, we tend to focus more on the bottom of the picture"
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 479.625,
      "end": 481.73,
      "duration": 2.105,
      "text": "than the top of the picture, and that's what this class"
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 481.73,
      "end": 483.45,
      "duration": 1.72,
      "text": "will focus on."
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 483.45,
      "end": 485.6,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "You run the risk that you'll forget there is a top of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 485.6,
      "end": 488.21,
      "duration": 2.61,
      "text": "picture, that there are ecosystems, there are"
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 488.21,
      "end": 491.0,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "organisms, physiology and all that."
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 491.0,
      "end": 491.62,
      "duration": 0.62,
      "text": "Oh well."
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 491.62,
      "end": 492.35,
      "duration": 0.73,
      "text": "What can I say?"
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 492.35,
      "end": 494.78,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "Why do we focus the bottom of the picture?"
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 494.78,
      "end": 497.45,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "Why do we focus so much on, say, the molecules of life?"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 497.45,
      "end": 501.46,
      "duration": 4.01,
      "text": "You're going to get a lot of molecules of life in the"
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 501.46,
      "end": 503.46,
      "duration": 2.0,
      "text": "beginning of this course."
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 503.46,
      "end": 504.92,
      "duration": 1.46,
      "text": "We're going to focus on--"
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 504.92,
      "end": 506.75,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "we'll think about organelles and cells."
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 506.75,
      "end": 509.5,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "You'll hear less about tissues, less about organs,"
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 509.5,
      "end": 512.28,
      "duration": 2.78,
      "text": "less about organisms as a whole."
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 512.28,
      "end": 520.36,
      "duration": 8.08,
      "text": "And the reason is life is most universal down at its bottom."
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 520.36,
      "end": 523.289,
      "duration": 2.929,
      "text": "That is what's shared across all life."
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 523.289,
      "end": 526.42,
      "duration": 3.131,
      "text": "Rather than, say, focus on the glorious, wonderful"
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 526.42,
      "end": 530.02,
      "duration": 3.6,
      "text": "differences between all the different phyla and learning"
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 530.02,
      "end": 532.57,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "all sorts of genuses and of all sorts of interesting--"
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 532.57,
      "end": 535.55,
      "duration": 2.98,
      "text": "we want to focus on that which is most universal."
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 535.55,
      "end": 536.75,
      "duration": 1.2,
      "text": "Now, there are some differences."
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 536.75,
      "end": 539.08,
      "duration": 2.33,
      "text": "We will look differently at microbe, prokaryotes versus"
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 539.08,
      "end": 540.6,
      "duration": 1.52,
      "text": "eukaryotes and all."
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 540.6,
      "end": 543.88,
      "duration": 3.28,
      "text": "But for the most part, what we're trying to do is ask what"
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 543.88,
      "end": 549.71,
      "duration": 5.83,
      "text": "are universal principles that apply across all organisms?"
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 549.71,
      "end": 552.09,
      "duration": 2.38,
      "text": "What are the ways organisms are built up?"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 552.09,
      "end": 554.91,
      "duration": 2.82,
      "text": "Commonalities, like the genetic code, that applies"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 554.91,
      "end": 557.92,
      "duration": 3.01,
      "text": "pretty broadly across all organisms, commonalities of"
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 557.92,
      "end": 560.5,
      "duration": 2.58,
      "text": "signalling systems, regulatory systems."
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 560.5,
      "end": 562.86,
      "duration": 2.36,
      "text": "Things like that are what we're most interested in,"
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 562.86,
      "end": 565.91,
      "duration": 3.05,
      "text": "because once you learn that, it's much easier to layer on"
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 565.91,
      "end": 568.75,
      "duration": 2.84,
      "text": "top of it the differences, the unique differences, that makes"
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 568.75,
      "end": 572.83,
      "duration": 4.08,
      "text": "a fruit fly a fruit fly or a tree a tree."
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 572.83,
      "end": 576.68,
      "duration": 3.85,
      "text": "So anyway, that's our perspective on it, and I hope"
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 576.68,
      "end": 577.69,
      "duration": 1.01,
      "text": "you like it."
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 577.69,
      "end": 580.97,
      "duration": 3.28,
      "text": "But it's the only prospective we've got, so there you go."
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 580.97,
      "end": 584.55,
      "duration": 3.58,
      "text": "Next, a few dates to keep in mind."
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 587.54,
      "end": 591.75,
      "duration": 4.21,
      "text": "Important dates in the history of life."
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 591.75,
      "end": 597.55,
      "duration": 5.8,
      "text": "Again to provide perspective, we're not going to focus on"
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 597.55,
      "end": 599.84,
      "duration": 2.29,
      "text": "lots of them, but a few that you should know."
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 599.84,
      "end": 603.52,
      "duration": 3.68,
      "text": "About 4.0 billion years ago--"
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 603.52,
      "end": 606.0,
      "duration": 2.48,
      "text": "BYA means billion years ago--"
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 606.0,
      "end": 607.25,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "the earth cooled."
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 610.05,
      "end": 612.37,
      "duration": 2.32,
      "text": "Before that, it was a hot, molten mass."
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 612.37,
      "end": 616.23,
      "duration": 3.86,
      "text": "There until it cooled, there was no real prospect of life."
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 616.23,
      "end": 619.04,
      "duration": 2.81,
      "text": "One of the things I find absolutely wonderful is that"
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 619.04,
      "end": 624.29,
      "duration": 5.25,
      "text": "by 3.7 billion years ago, there was clear evidence of"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 624.29,
      "end": 626.94,
      "duration": 2.65,
      "text": "the first life."
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 626.94,
      "end": 628.61,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "Whatever it was, it didn't take that all"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 628.61,
      "end": 630.25,
      "duration": 1.64,
      "text": "long to get life going."
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 630.25,
      "end": 634.17,
      "duration": 3.92,
      "text": "Somehow, it can't be that hard, although I got to say we"
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 634.17,
      "end": 635.54,
      "duration": 1.37,
      "text": "don't quite understand all of it."
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 635.54,
      "end": 638.47,
      "duration": 2.93,
      "text": "Increasingly, people are looking back to how early life"
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 638.47,
      "end": 641.18,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "can form out of prebiotic materials."
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 641.18,
      "end": 647.31,
      "duration": 6.13,
      "text": "And these things were prokaryotic organisms, like"
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 647.31,
      "end": 651.79,
      "duration": 4.48,
      "text": "bacteria, and they played a very important role, for"
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 651.79,
      "end": 656.0,
      "duration": 4.21,
      "text": "example, in changing the entire atmosphere of the earth"
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 656.0,
      "end": 659.45,
      "duration": 3.45,
      "text": "to contain oxygen, which made possible other things."
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 659.45,
      "end": 660.33,
      "duration": 0.88,
      "text": "So--"
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 660.33,
      "end": 663.53,
      "duration": 3.2,
      "text": "sorry, in shaping the content of oxygen in the atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 663.53,
      "end": 670.06,
      "duration": 6.53,
      "text": "So 1.5 billion years ago, one has a totally amazing"
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 670.06,
      "end": 674.63,
      "duration": 4.57,
      "text": "invention, which is the first nucleated cells."
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 674.63,
      "end": 677.06,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "These bacteria lack nuclei."
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 677.06,
      "end": 679.11,
      "duration": 2.05,
      "text": "Here we have nucleated cells, eukaryotes."
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 684.18,
      "end": 690.01,
      "duration": 5.83,
      "text": "Major event, and it occurred because of a fusion of two of"
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 690.01,
      "end": 692.65,
      "duration": 2.64,
      "text": "these prokaryotic-type cells."
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 692.65,
      "end": 696.46,
      "duration": 3.81,
      "text": "One takes up residence in the other, and there is a"
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 696.46,
      "end": 698.97,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "symbiosis between two cells and that gave"
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 698.97,
      "end": 701.39,
      "duration": 2.42,
      "text": "rise to your nucleus."
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 701.39,
      "end": 704.03,
      "duration": 2.64,
      "text": "The one that lives inside the other eventually discarded"
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 704.03,
      "end": 706.52,
      "duration": 2.49,
      "text": "most of its functions there."
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 706.52,
      "end": 707.56,
      "duration": 1.04,
      "text": "Sorry--"
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 707.56,
      "end": 711.15,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "yes, that gave rise to a nucleated cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 711.15,
      "end": 715.58,
      "duration": 4.43,
      "text": "It's a fusion between two different prokaryotic"
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 715.58,
      "end": 718.73,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "organisms that had different properties, one of which is"
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 718.73,
      "end": 721.04,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "the nucleated cell, the other of which you see in the"
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 721.04,
      "end": 722.89,
      "duration": 1.85,
      "text": "mitochondria, for example."
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 722.89,
      "end": 726.06,
      "duration": 3.17,
      "text": "There's still a genome in the mitochondria, for example."
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 726.06,
      "end": 729.42,
      "duration": 3.36,
      "text": "And so we can recognize that there was this prokaryotic"
    },
    {
      "index": 192,
      "start": 729.42,
      "end": 731.62,
      "duration": 2.2,
      "text": "fusion event."
    },
    {
      "index": 193,
      "start": 731.62,
      "end": 734.96,
      "duration": 3.34,
      "text": "Notice it took 2 billion years, more than two billion"
    },
    {
      "index": 194,
      "start": 734.96,
      "end": 739.76,
      "duration": 4.8,
      "text": "years, to make eukaryotes and only 300 million years to make"
    },
    {
      "index": 195,
      "start": 739.76,
      "end": 741.37,
      "duration": 1.61,
      "text": "the first life."
    },
    {
      "index": 196,
      "start": 741.37,
      "end": 743.3,
      "duration": 1.93,
      "text": "I find that quite remarkable."
    },
    {
      "index": 197,
      "start": 743.3,
      "end": 745.33,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "What does that tell us?"
    },
    {
      "index": 198,
      "start": 745.33,
      "end": 748.86,
      "duration": 3.53,
      "text": "That it was that much harder to make a eukaryotic cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 199,
      "start": 748.86,
      "end": 750.17,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "Maybe."
    },
    {
      "index": 200,
      "start": 750.17,
      "end": 753.14,
      "duration": 2.97,
      "text": "Or maybe it tells us about the power of competition."
    },
    {
      "index": 201,
      "start": 753.14,
      "end": 755.4,
      "duration": 2.26,
      "text": "Once you have some life--"
    },
    {
      "index": 202,
      "start": 755.4,
      "end": 758.28,
      "duration": 2.88,
      "text": "that the first prokaryotic cells-- it's so much harder to"
    },
    {
      "index": 203,
      "start": 758.28,
      "end": 760.85,
      "duration": 2.57,
      "text": "get anything else that can come in and compete with it,"
    },
    {
      "index": 204,
      "start": 760.85,
      "end": 762.16,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "because it has to be better."
    },
    {
      "index": 205,
      "start": 762.16,
      "end": 763.953,
      "duration": 1.793,
      "text": "Maybe the first life didn't have to compete with anything,"
    },
    {
      "index": 206,
      "start": 763.953,
      "end": 765.17,
      "duration": 1.217,
      "text": "and it was easy."
    },
    {
      "index": 207,
      "start": 765.17,
      "end": 768.1,
      "duration": 2.93,
      "text": "And then in an innovation like the eukaryotic cell, well,"
    },
    {
      "index": 208,
      "start": 768.1,
      "end": 770.38,
      "duration": 2.28,
      "text": "maybe that was a lot harder to accomplish, because it had to"
    },
    {
      "index": 209,
      "start": 770.38,
      "end": 774.24,
      "duration": 3.86,
      "text": "be better than the prokaryotic cells it was competing with."
    },
    {
      "index": 210,
      "start": 774.24,
      "end": 777.16,
      "duration": 2.92,
      "text": "I'm not sure, but I find that difference in time to be kind"
    },
    {
      "index": 211,
      "start": 777.16,
      "end": 778.89,
      "duration": 1.73,
      "text": "of a remarkably interesting thing."
    },
    {
      "index": 212,
      "start": 778.89,
      "end": 782.25,
      "duration": 3.36,
      "text": "That that was short, and that took a lot longer."
    },
    {
      "index": 213,
      "start": 782.25,
      "end": 787.76,
      "duration": 5.51,
      "text": "0.5 billion years ago, roughly speaking, what you have are"
    },
    {
      "index": 214,
      "start": 787.76,
      "end": 790.47,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "multicellular organisms with body plans."
    },
    {
      "index": 215,
      "start": 793.93,
      "end": 797.62,
      "duration": 3.69,
      "text": "Up to this point, you have single-celled organisms."
    },
    {
      "index": 216,
      "start": 797.62,
      "end": 800.19,
      "duration": 2.57,
      "text": "Now you get multicellular organisms with body plans."
    },
    {
      "index": 217,
      "start": 800.19,
      "end": 804.15,
      "duration": 3.96,
      "text": "And another remarkable thing, once body plans, multicellular"
    },
    {
      "index": 218,
      "start": 804.15,
      "end": 807.7,
      "duration": 3.55,
      "text": "body plans, are invented, they explode very quickly."
    },
    {
      "index": 219,
      "start": 807.7,
      "end": 812.38,
      "duration": 4.68,
      "text": "Somehow it was hard to invent multicellularity, to get cells"
    },
    {
      "index": 220,
      "start": 812.38,
      "end": 815.23,
      "duration": 2.85,
      "text": "to work together and be an organism, but once it was"
    },
    {
      "index": 221,
      "start": 815.23,
      "end": 819.51,
      "duration": 4.28,
      "text": "invented, it was not hard to diversify it into zillions of"
    },
    {
      "index": 222,
      "start": 819.51,
      "end": 821.39,
      "duration": 1.88,
      "text": "different body plans and forms."
    },
    {
      "index": 223,
      "start": 821.39,
      "end": 823.35,
      "duration": 1.96,
      "text": "That tells us something."
    },
    {
      "index": 224,
      "start": 823.35,
      "end": 826.86,
      "duration": 3.51,
      "text": "That as soon as we see multicellularity, we start"
    },
    {
      "index": 225,
      "start": 826.86,
      "end": 828.64,
      "duration": 1.78,
      "text": "seeing huge numbers of different body"
    },
    {
      "index": 226,
      "start": 828.64,
      "end": 830.01,
      "duration": 1.37,
      "text": "plans pretty quickly."
    },
    {
      "index": 227,
      "start": 830.01,
      "end": 831.27,
      "duration": 1.26,
      "text": "Very interesting."
    },
    {
      "index": 228,
      "start": 831.27,
      "end": 832.65,
      "duration": 1.38,
      "text": "A few other important dates."
    },
    {
      "index": 229,
      "start": 832.65,
      "end": 833.8,
      "duration": 1.15,
      "text": "Two other dates."
    },
    {
      "index": 230,
      "start": 833.8,
      "end": 841.68,
      "duration": 7.88,
      "text": "0.005 billion years ago are humans."
    },
    {
      "index": 231,
      "start": 841.68,
      "end": 844.5,
      "duration": 2.82,
      "text": "Just to put yourself in your place on this scale."
    },
    {
      "index": 232,
      "start": 844.5,
      "end": 856.695,
      "duration": 12.195,
      "text": "And 0.00000015 billion years ago, MIT was founded."
    },
    {
      "index": 233,
      "start": 859.26,
      "end": 862.4,
      "duration": 3.14,
      "text": "Just to put this in prospective."
    },
    {
      "index": 234,
      "start": 862.4,
      "end": 864.71,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "index": 235,
      "start": 864.71,
      "end": 868.68,
      "duration": 3.97,
      "text": "Couple of other things you should know."
    },
    {
      "index": 236,
      "start": 868.68,
      "end": 871.9,
      "duration": 3.22,
      "text": "The types of cells I've been referring to."
    },
    {
      "index": 237,
      "start": 876.36,
      "end": 878.83,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "There's really two fundamental types of cells."
    },
    {
      "index": 238,
      "start": 878.83,
      "end": 880.57,
      "duration": 1.74,
      "text": "And I've been using the word already."
    },
    {
      "index": 239,
      "start": 880.57,
      "end": 882.9,
      "duration": 2.33,
      "text": "Let me just get it out there."
    },
    {
      "index": 240,
      "start": 882.9,
      "end": 884.15,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "Prokaryotes."
    },
    {
      "index": 241,
      "start": 885.82,
      "end": 887.07,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "Eukaryotes."
    },
    {
      "index": 242,
      "start": 891.74,
      "end": 894.506,
      "duration": 2.766,
      "text": "Karyo refers to nucleus."
    },
    {
      "index": 243,
      "start": 898.03,
      "end": 899.81,
      "duration": 1.78,
      "text": "Eu- means true."
    },
    {
      "index": 244,
      "start": 899.81,
      "end": 902.88,
      "duration": 3.07,
      "text": "Pro- means primitive, before."
    },
    {
      "index": 245,
      "start": 902.88,
      "end": 905.555,
      "duration": 2.675,
      "text": "So eukaryotic cells--"
    },
    {
      "index": 246,
      "start": 909.01,
      "end": 911.73,
      "duration": 2.72,
      "text": "you're, by the way, a eukaryote."
    },
    {
      "index": 247,
      "start": 911.73,
      "end": 912.88,
      "duration": 1.15,
      "text": "Right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 248,
      "start": 912.88,
      "end": 914.95,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "Just in case you haven't read the owner's manual, you're"
    },
    {
      "index": 249,
      "start": 914.95,
      "end": 917.68,
      "duration": 2.73,
      "text": "eukaryotes."
    },
    {
      "index": 250,
      "start": 917.68,
      "end": 919.52,
      "duration": 1.84,
      "text": "--have true nuclei."
    },
    {
      "index": 251,
      "start": 919.52,
      "end": 925.23,
      "duration": 5.71,
      "text": "Inside the nucleus, there's your DNA, which is organized"
    },
    {
      "index": 252,
      "start": 925.23,
      "end": 927.47,
      "duration": 2.24,
      "text": "better than I just drew it there, because, in fact, it's"
    },
    {
      "index": 253,
      "start": 927.47,
      "end": 929.76,
      "duration": 2.29,
      "text": "very, very long and has to be packed up well."
    },
    {
      "index": 254,
      "start": 929.76,
      "end": 933.25,
      "duration": 3.49,
      "text": "It'll have organelles like mitochondria."
    },
    {
      "index": 255,
      "start": 933.25,
      "end": 934.78,
      "duration": 1.53,
      "text": "It could have chloroplasts."
    },
    {
      "index": 256,
      "start": 934.78,
      "end": 936.39,
      "duration": 1.61,
      "text": "It could have other organelles."
    },
    {
      "index": 257,
      "start": 936.39,
      "end": 938.41,
      "duration": 2.02,
      "text": "It'll have other things we'll talk about--"
    },
    {
      "index": 258,
      "start": 938.41,
      "end": 940.59,
      "duration": 2.18,
      "text": "Golgi apparatuses and endoplasmic"
    },
    {
      "index": 259,
      "start": 940.59,
      "end": 943.37,
      "duration": 2.78,
      "text": "reticula and all that."
    },
    {
      "index": 260,
      "start": 943.37,
      "end": 947.14,
      "duration": 3.77,
      "text": "Bacteria don't have a true nucleus."
    },
    {
      "index": 261,
      "start": 947.14,
      "end": 950.31,
      "duration": 3.17,
      "text": "It's not that they're DNA isn't somehow organized, but"
    },
    {
      "index": 262,
      "start": 950.31,
      "end": 952.6,
      "duration": 2.29,
      "text": "it doesn't have a true nucleus with the wall around it."
    },
    {
      "index": 263,
      "start": 952.6,
      "end": 955.14,
      "duration": 2.54,
      "text": "There's no wall around that nucleus like that."
    },
    {
      "index": 264,
      "start": 955.14,
      "end": 957.79,
      "duration": 2.65,
      "text": "They often have interesting cell walls."
    },
    {
      "index": 265,
      "start": 957.79,
      "end": 960.52,
      "duration": 2.73,
      "text": "A striking thing, although I've drawn them as the same"
    },
    {
      "index": 266,
      "start": 960.52,
      "end": 963.25,
      "duration": 2.73,
      "text": "size, these are much smaller."
    },
    {
      "index": 267,
      "start": 963.25,
      "end": 967.73,
      "duration": 4.48,
      "text": "These are 1 to 2 microns."
    },
    {
      "index": 268,
      "start": 967.73,
      "end": 973.57,
      "duration": 5.84,
      "text": "These, 10 to 40 microns in diameter."
    },
    {
      "index": 269,
      "start": 973.57,
      "end": 978.4,
      "duration": 4.83,
      "text": "And so that means that if we talk about volume, we cube it."
    },
    {
      "index": 270,
      "start": 978.4,
      "end": 982.05,
      "duration": 3.65,
      "text": "So the volumes of these guys are something like 1,000 to"
    },
    {
      "index": 271,
      "start": 982.05,
      "end": 984.93,
      "duration": 2.88,
      "text": "60,000 times bigger."
    },
    {
      "index": 272,
      "start": 984.93,
      "end": 990.09,
      "duration": 5.16,
      "text": "Eukaryotic cells are large compared to prokaryotic cells."
    },
    {
      "index": 273,
      "start": 990.09,
      "end": 994.13,
      "duration": 4.04,
      "text": "Now, remember these are the guys who were early."
    },
    {
      "index": 274,
      "start": 994.13,
      "end": 995.77,
      "duration": 1.64,
      "text": "These guys come along later."
    },
    {
      "index": 275,
      "start": 995.77,
      "end": 997.65,
      "duration": 1.88,
      "text": "And there are important differences that we'll talk"
    },
    {
      "index": 276,
      "start": 997.65,
      "end": 1002.38,
      "duration": 4.73,
      "text": "about in eukaryotic and prokaryotic cells."
    },
    {
      "index": 277,
      "start": 1002.38,
      "end": 1005.78,
      "duration": 3.4,
      "text": "You're a eukaryote, all animals, all plants are"
    },
    {
      "index": 278,
      "start": 1005.78,
      "end": 1006.68,
      "duration": 0.9,
      "text": "eukaryotes."
    },
    {
      "index": 279,
      "start": 1006.68,
      "end": 1009.5,
      "duration": 2.82,
      "text": "Fungi, such as yeast, et cetera."
    }
  ],
